    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point, boasting a massive 80.98 efficiency score. His matchup against Ober is elevated by a favorable park factor and a 19% boost from the opposing starter's xERA, but the real differentiator is the 87% stolen base success rate against Ober\u2019s delivery, making **Pete Crow-Armstrong** a critical engine for our most scarce category. **Christian Yelich** (74.22) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) round out our top-tier tier of starters; **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon edge and the leadoff spot, while **Kazuma Okamoto** capitalizes on Kay\u2019s inflated 4.67 xERA, providing a high-floor anchor at first base.\n\nWhile we remain bullish on our outfield, we are monitoring the volatility of the back-end spots. **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) and **Nelson Velazquez** (59.84) are both in prime positions to exploit the weak 5.29 xERA of Merrill Kelly, assuming their projected lineup spots hold true. Conversely, the bench decision regarding **Casey Schmitt** (42.63) was the most difficult; while he narrowly missed the starting cut, his negative park factor and a tough matchup against Miller forced the optimizer to favor the higher offensive ceilings of **Junior Caminero** (58.95) and **Yordan Alvarez** (56.17). Despite **Yordan Alvarez** facing a slightly tougher pitcher in Kremer, his elite xwOBA of 0.475 makes him a non-negotiable start regardless of the SP xERA. We advise cautious management of **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Nelson Velazquez**, as their sub-50 to mid-50 scores are contingent on \"Lineup Pending\" confirmations; any shift down the order or a late scratch could trigger a benching to preserve our season-long game caps.",
